From b96738d0030dd098a3a5856db16c3cfd8c301ce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:56:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] GOLD fast credit: own rate-limit budget, visible
 fallback reason, retry from "check original credit"

The owner's first live fast-credit purchase (order 0xacecd436..., tx 0xec38fd54..., mined 16:40:11 UTC) fell
back to finality: the receipt verifies (replayed locally through fastCreditTopup with the production row and
the real receipt: credited), so the polls were refused before reaching it. They shared the per-IP
'world-gold:' ECONOMY_LIMITER budget (20/min) with the panel's ledger refreshes and the AIMarket pane's
15 s status polls during the same purchase.

- world-gold-api: fast-credit uses its own key 'world-gold-fast:<ip>' (12 polls in its first minute).
- worker: each fast-credit outcome is logged (status or refusal code only) for live tails.
- fastGoldCredit: the schedule's end names its last transient answer (TIMEOUT_WAITING, TIMEOUT_RATE_LIMITED,
  ...); a fallback can be restarted, never doubled; the follow keeps its transaction hash.
- GoldPurchase: the fallback message shows the reference code; "Check original credit" retries the fast
  credit too. The review button now says what it does: "Next: check allowance" (it prompts nothing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
